[engl]
{100}{}{Aradesh}
{200}{}{You see Aradesh.}
{1000}{}{Predialogue installations}
{1010}{}{[First visit]}
{1020}{}{[2nd visit]}
{2000}{}{Greetings, wanderer. Please do not be offended if the gentlefolk about seem rude. As Dharma said, 'Tough times tan the human hide.' Your business in Shady Sands might be?}
{2010}{}{I'm from a small village west of here. I'm just
 exploring and mean you no harm.}
{2020}{}{What's it to you?}
{2030}{}{My reasons are mine to keep.}
{2040}{}{I'm from a Vault to the west. My people are dying of thirst and I need to find a water purifier chip  for them to survive.}
{2050}{}{I'm saving an entire people from destruction!}
{2060}{}{Shady Sands? Whoops, I'm lost! I'll just be going now.}
{2070}{}{Hunh?}
{3000}{}{I know of no village to the west.}
{3010}{}{Have you been through the mountains west of here?}
{3020}{}{So?}
{3030}{}{Are you saying you know every location from here  to the ocean?}
{3040}{}{I'm sure you've been many places, but you must have
 missed my tiny village.}
{4000}{}{Ah well, to my regret, I have not. Which begs the question,  how did you make that passage?}
{4010}{}{It was pretty tough, but I made it.}
{5000}{}{Yes, hmmm, yes, yes. yes. I shall believe you...for now.  But we do not trust easily, especially those who might be dangerous. Know that Seth and I will be watching you.}
{5010}{}{[Done.]}
{6000}{}{Greetings again, young wanderer. I hope your stay here has been pleasant.}
{6010}{}{It's been great. Can I ask you some questions?}
{6020}{}{It has. I gotta run though.}
{6030}{}{If you like sewers.}
{6040}{}{Nuh-huh.}
{7000}{}{Certainly. What do you wish to know?}
{7010}{}{Can you tell me about Shady Sands?}
{7020}{}{What can you tell me about the other towns around here?}
{7030}{}{What's going on around here?}
{7040}{}{Thanks. Bye.}
{8000}{}{It is my town, wanderer. You must answer my questions  
> or leave. This is not a matter of choice.}
{8010}{}{I don't have to tell you anything.}
{8020}{}{I mean you no harm, really.}
{8030}{}{Don't worry, I'm leaving.}
{9000}{}{You are quite insolent. I believe you should leave. Do not return. You will not be welcome.}
{9010}{}{[Done.]}
{10000}{}{So be it, wanderer. Seth will show you out.}
{10010}{}{[Done.]}
{11000}{}{Shady Sands is much like a family, one that keeps  to itself.}
{11010}{}{Interesting. Are there any other cities around here?}
{11020}{}{What kind of things do you have around here?}
{11030}{}{How cute. Well, I better be going.}
{12000}{}{The Gardens are on the south side. The Brahma Pens are north, although the smell is, I fear, quite intense this time of year.}
{12010}{}{Thanks. Can I ask you a few more questions?}
{12020}{}{Thanks. Bye.}
{13000}{}{Junktown lies south of here, though there is little in  the way of visitation. From stories, I'm certain there  are cities south of that.}
{13010}{}{Thanks. I . . . Can I ask you a few more questions?}
{14000}{}{Oh my yes. Great packs of Rad Scorpions are killing  our herds. We don't know where they're from, and no matter how many we kill, there's always more!}
{14010}{}{Go on.}
{15000}{}{And now the monsters are attacking my people! Razlo is trying to find a cure for their poison, but I'm not sure how it goes.}
{15010}{}{Well, I'll help you get rid of these things!}
{15020}{}{I can help you for a price.}
{15030}{}{That's terrible. Can I ask you a few more questions?}
{16000}{}{Ummm, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes! Please talk to Razlo. He possesses far more information on these creatures than I.}
{16010}{}{[Done.]}

